.TH smi-docker-build "1" "November 2026" "SMI Toolset" "SMI Docker Command"
.SH NAME
smi-docker-build \- Build and tag a Docker image
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smi-docker-build
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B smi-docker-build
is the second step of the Docker build process of the toolset:
.BR smi-docker-prepare (1),
.BR smi-docker-build ,
.BR smi-docker-push (1).
It sources the \fBdocker.sh\fR library and the \fBbuild.sh\fR script of the current directory, and
builds the image locally. It pushes nothing, so the image can be checked or run before
.BR smi-docker-push (1)
publishes it.
.PP
The steps are:
.IP 1.
\fBdocker_build\fR: the function of \fBbuild.sh\fR, for the work before the build.
.IP 2.
\fBbuild_image\fR: \fBdocker build\fR of \fBDOCKER_FILE\fR with the current directory as context, as
\fIDOCKER_ID_ORGANIZATION\fB/\fIDOCKER_PROJECT_NAME\fB:\fIDOCKER_PROJECT_VERSION\fR,
with BuildKit and plain progress output, and the build arguments \fBVERSION\fR, \fBBUILD_DATE\fR,
\fBVCS_REF\fR, the short \fBgit\fR commit, and every variable named in \fBDOCKER_BUILD_ARGS\fR.
A variable named there that is empty stops the build.
.IP 3.
\fBbuild_latest_tag\fR: tags the image also as \fBlatest\fR.
.IP 4.
\fBbuild_inspect_latest_tag\fR: \fBdocker inspect\fR of the \fBlatest\fR tag.
.IP 5.
\fBbuild_show_images\fR: lists the local images.
.PP
Each step runs while the previous one succeeds. Steps 2 to 5 run only when \fBDOCKER_FILE\fR exists, so a directory of several images has a \fBbuild.sh\fR whose \fBdocker_build\fR runs
\fBsmi-docker-build\fR in each image directory.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Set by \fBbuild.sh\fR:
.TP
\fBDOCKER_ID_ORGANIZATION\fR
Docker registry organization or user, \fBsetmyinfo\fR by default.
.TP
\fBDOCKER_PROJECT_NAME\fR
Name of the image, the name of the current directory by default.
.TP
\fBDOCKER_PROJECT_VERSION\fR
Version tag of the image.
.TP
\fBDOCKER_BUILD_ARGS\fR
Names of further variables passed as build arguments, empty by default. For example
\fBDOCKER_BUILD_ARGS="JDK_VERSION"\fR after \fBincludePackages jdk\fR passes the version of the
package file, so the \fBDockerfile\fR declares \fBARG JDK_VERSION\fR without a value.
.TP
\fBDOCKER_FILE\fR
The \fBDockerfile\fR, \fBDockerfile\fR of the current directory by default. For example
\fBDOCKER_FILE=src/main/docker/Dockerfile\fR keeps \fBbuild.sh\fR in the project root, and the
\fBDockerfile\fR copies from the project, such as \fBtarget/\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ./build.sh
Sets the variables above, and defines \fBdocker_prepare\fR and \fBdocker_build\fR when they have
work to do; both do nothing by default.
.TP
.I DOCKER_FILE
The image definition.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit status of the last step that ran, so a failed build fails the command.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
The whole process, from the directory of \fBbuild.sh\fR:
.RS
.nf
smi-docker-prepare
smi-docker-build
smi-docker-push
.fi
.RE
.SH AUTHOR
.PP
Command written by Imre Tabur.
